{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Work and Play", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Reported Speech and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use reported speech (indirect speech) when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. <br/>In writing, it is common to use reported speech in storytelling and narrations. It allows the writer to share dialogue with the reader without always using quotation marks.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you tell people what someone has said you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past' since we are reporting the information at a later time. You need to change the verb to the next past form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">\u201cI'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming</span> to the party.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already</span> eaten.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> cook.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> cook.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "When you report what someone has said, you need to change the pronoun. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't like chocolate\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I said, \u201cI don't like chocolate.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I</span></span> didn't like chocolate.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Bill said, \u201cI don't like chocolate.\u201d  >  Bill said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">he</span></span> didn't like chocolate.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to report questions asked, the subject normally comes before the verb.<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>: Where is the sun?<br/><span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>: The wind asked <span class=\"strong\">where the sun was</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When the question is a yes/no questions, you use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">whether</span> to report it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The sun asks <span class=\"strong\">if</span>/<span class=\"strong\">whether</span> the wind would be around without shifting temperatures.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal May\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use tag questions to clarify or confirm whether of no something is true.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are used to:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">confirm whether or not something is true</span>, or", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">to show you expect a reply</span> from the person you are talking to to.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes'<br/><ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you</span>? <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</span><li> <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"2\"> A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> question tag. Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'<br/>  <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you</span>?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</span> </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"italic\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same.<br/>For <span class=\"italic\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do/does</span> or <span class=\"italic\">did/didn'</span>t. Look at the examples in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "It is important, isn't it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You are finished with that, aren't you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You didn't go to work on Sunday afternoon, did you Peter? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You went downtown to another bistro, didn't you?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pitiful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "deserving or causing feelings of pity or sympathy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We always support you and your little pitiful problems with romance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you are angry with someone.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hush", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a person become quiet, or still", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why don't you hush and listen to me?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have your back", "type": "name"}, {"content": "if somebody \"always has your back\" it means that they are always there to support you", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We always have your back.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make a scene", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a public disturbance or excited emotional display", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are making a scene.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to scram", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go abruptly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Get out of here! Scram! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hit the bricks ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an impolite way of saying go away", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Scram! Peter. Hit the bricks! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch a TED TALK on a topic you find interesting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Watch it a couple of times and take notes on the important information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the interactive transcript to select three important direct quotes from the TED Talk.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a brief summary of the talk and include the three direct quotes in your article as indirect speech.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I practice listening for gist and for detail.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes on my TED TALK topic.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I skim and scan for information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a brief summary of the talk.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, friendship and reaction in different situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can quote other people.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can ask for clarification and ask for someone's opinion.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you ever watched a TED TALK video? If yes, which one?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What are your favorite TED TALK topics to watch?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "corre